# XCU what
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.what.001
anchor     utilities/what.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/what.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       what writes the pathname, then each string after @(#) up to a
           double quote, >, newline, backslash, NUL or end of file, each
           preceded by a tab.
test       t/001-strings.sh

assertion  XCU.what.002
anchor     utilities/what.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -s writes at most one string per file.
test       t/002-option-s.sh

assertion  XCU.what.003
anchor     utilities/what.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/what.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A file without a match gives the pathname line and status 1; so
           does a nonexistent file.
test       t/003-no-match.sh

assertion  XCU.what.004
anchor     utilities/what.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/what.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Each file operand gets its own heading and strings, in operand
           order, and the status is 0 if any file matched.
test       t/004-several-files.sh

assertion  XCU.what.005
anchor     utilities/what.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Text retrieved with the %W% keyword is found by what.
test       t/005-with-get.sh
